@startuml 04_mutex_how_it_works
title 4. How a mutex works (std::mutex, Experiment 2)
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

start
partition "lock()" {
  :try to change state 0 to 1\n(one atomic CAS);
  if (state was 0?) then (yes: got it)
    :fast path\nno kernel involved;
  else (no: another thread holds it)
    :mark the lock as contended;
    :futex_wait()\nSLEEP in the kernel;
    :woken up, retry the lock;
  endif
}
:critical section\n++counter;
partition "unlock()" {
  :set state back to 0\n(atomic exchange);
  if (anyone marked it contended?) then (yes)
    :futex_wake()\nsyscall: wake one sleeper;
  else (no)
    :nothing else to do;
  endif
}
stop

footer Uncontended lock+unlock is about 4 ns with no kernel call. Under contention the futex syscalls are the cost.
@enduml
